    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans, while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 helper that formats an E.164 number as `country code, space, national digits grouped in threes` (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). The country-code split mirrors `E164Telephone` (`+1` = 1 digit, otherwise 2, matching the app's `+61` default), and it returns non-E.164 input unchanged.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` response schema (raw `telephone` stays E.164).\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired `telephoneDisplay` via `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner)`, derived at read time, following the existing computed-field pattern.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
